{"id":"19407d9b9232e9e7794f09fb8fdd3248e6fa3031","axis":"silent","repo":"kestra-io/kestra","sha":"19407d9b9232e9e7794f09fb8fdd3248e6fa3031","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"ui/AGENTS.md","lines":["@@ -68,6 +68,7 @@ A design system rots fast if it's treated as a one-time deliverable. Apply these"," - Only expose props that are actually used somewhere in the codebase. Speculative props rot."," - Mirror Element Plus prop names where possible — predictability is a feature."," - Type a wrapper's props by extending the Element Plus interface (`interface KsInputProps extends Omit<InputProps, \"modelValue\">`) instead of copying them, and forward them with `usePassedProps`: Vue casts an omitted boolean to `false`, which would override defaults such as `validateEvent` or `teleported`.","+- Type the HTML attributes a wrapper forwards through `$attrs` with a `@vue-ignore` intersection, `defineProps<KsButtonProps & /* @vue-ignore */ Omit<NativeAttributes<ButtonHTMLAttributes>, keyof KsButtonProps>>()`: vue-tsc still checks every attribute a caller passes, while the compiler leaves them out of the runtime props so they stay in `$attrs`. `NativeAttributes` drops Vue's `on*` listener types, which would otherwise retype the wrapper's own events (`@change` receiving an `Event`). The type cannot see whether the template forwards them, so `htmlAttributes.test.ts` mounts each such wrapper and checks the attributes reach the DOM; add new wrappers to it."," - Pass `v-bind=\"$attrs\"` and forward slots so wrappers don't trap consumer extension points."," - Add the new component or prop to the relevant table in this file, plus a Storybook story and a unit test, in the same PR."," - Document tokens in code comments next to where they're declared in `ks-theme-*.css`. The `scripts/generate-palette.mjs` file is auto-generated — don't hand-edit it.","@@ -241,7 +242,7 @@ Rules:"," "," - All icons come from [`vue-material-design-icons`](https://github.com/robcresswell/vue-material-design-icons) via `<KsIcon>` (or `<KsIconButton>` for clickable icons)."," - Never inline raw SVG, font-icon classes, or emoji as UI state. If a needed icon is missing, propose adding it to the DS rather than dropping an SVG into a feature folder.","-- Pass `name` (the kebab-case Material name); size and color come from props or the surrounding token context — don't override with inline `style`.","+- Put the icon component in `KsIcon`'s default slot (`<KsIcon><InformationOutline /></KsIcon>`); `KsIcon` has no `name` prop. Size and color come from props or the surrounding token context — don't override with inline `style`."," - **One icon per action, in OSS and EE alike.** Before picking an icon for an action (delete, edit, save, run, import…), follow the pattern already used for that action in the codebase: the icon most places use for it, not a variant of it."," - **Two file-type icon sets coexist on purpose, so don't merge them.** `fileUtils.fileIcon()` (behind `KsFileTag`) maps an extension to a monochrome `vue-material-design-icons` component, which inherits `--ks-icon-*` and so recolors per theme and per tag variant. `ui/src/components/utils/icons/Type.vue` renders the colored `material-file-icons` SVGs for the namespace file explorer, where the brand colors are the point. That package is a `ui/` dependency the design system does not have, and it bakes its colors into a base64 `<img>` that no token can reach, so it cannot be used from a `Ks*` component."," ","@@ -368,7 +369,7 @@ If your `<style>` block needs to exist:"," | Component | Purpose |"," |-----------|---------|"," | `KsButton` / `KsButtonGroup` | Primary action button and grouped buttons; `--ks-button-content-width` stretches the content (default `auto`); `block` stretches the button to its container's width; renders as a link with `tag=\"a\"` + `href` / `target` / `rel`, or `:tag=\"RouterLink\"` + `to` and `replace` |","-| `KsIcon` / `KsIconButton` | Material Design icon display; icon-only button (always with `aria-label`) |","+| `KsIcon` / `KsIconButton` | Material Design icon display (the icon component goes in the default slot); icon-only button (always with `aria-label`), which takes `KsButton`'s `type` |"," | `KsLink` | Styled hyperlink |"," | `KsText` | Typography wrapper — preferred over raw `<span>` / `<p>` for theme-aware text; `type=\"secondary\"` for muted text |"," | `KsScrollbar` | Custom-styled scrollbar wrapper |"],"additions":3,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"ui/packages/design-system/src/components/Basic/KsButton/KsButton.vue","lines":["@@ -5,8 +5,7 @@","         v-bind=\"tooltipPlacement ? {placement: tooltipPlacement} : {}\"","     >","         <ElButton","-            :aria-label=\"tooltip\"","-            v-bind=\"({...filteredProps(), ...$attrs})\"","+            v-bind=\"({'aria-label': tooltip, ...filteredProps(), ...$attrs})\"","             :class=\"{'is-square': square, 'is-block': block, 'kel-button--toned': tone}\"","             @click=\"emit('click', $event)\"","             plain","@@ -77,7 +76,8 @@"," </script>"," "," <script setup lang=\"ts\">","-    import {computed} from \"vue\"","+    import type {NativeAttributes} from \"../../../utils/nativeAttributes\"","+    import {computed, type ButtonHTMLAttributes, type AnchorHTMLAttributes} from \"vue\""," ","     import {ElButton} from \"element-plus\""," ","@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@","     defineOptions({inheritAttrs: false})"," ","     // Left undefined so a plain button does not render a replace=\"false\" attribute.","-    const props = withDefaults(defineProps<KsButtonProps>(), {replace: undefined})","+    const props = withDefaults(defineProps<KsButtonProps & /* @vue-ignore */ Omit<NativeAttributes<ButtonHTMLAttributes & Pick<AnchorHTMLAttributes, \"download\">>, keyof KsButtonProps>>(), {replace: undefined})"," ","     const emit = defineEmits<{","         click: [evt: MouseEvent]"],"additions":4,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"ui/packages/design-system/src/components/Basic/KsIcon.vu